1 OCCU gendarme du Roy et archer de la Compagnie de Gratien d’Aguerre, Gendarme du roi de France - Archer des ducs de Lorraine, Gendarme du Roy et archer de la  compagnie de Gratien d'Aguerre
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * Reference: [https://gw.geneanet.org/polka21?lang=en&pz=claudine&nz=maumert&ocz=0&p=robert&n=thier+r+y+de+saint+thomas Geneanet Genealogy] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Dec 1 2017,
2 CONC  14:53:56 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT from https://gw.geneanet.org/ntournoux?lang=fr&n=thiery+de+saint+thomas&p=robert+pierre
2 CONT
2 CONT Military
2 CONT Gendarme of the King, Archer of the King's Guards
2 CONT On May 15, 1509, he participated in the Battle of Agnadel (Italy-Lombardy) as a King's Archer in the Company of Gratien d'Aguerre, Lord of Vienne, Governor of Mouzon.
2 CONT Ennobled for military deeds on October 7, 1510, at the request of the knight Gratien d'Aguerre, by letters given to Bar le Duc by Antoine, Duke of Calabria and Lorraine, during the reign of Louis XII. Became Governor of Mouzon and
2 CONC  Lord of Vienne le Château (Saint Thomas de Vienne) in 1510.
2 CONT He participated brilliantly in the Battle of Ravenna on April 11, 1512, under the command of Gaston de Foix, Duke of Nemours, the king's 22-year-old nephew, who was killed in this battle. He was also killed in the Battle of Marign
2 CONC an on September 15, 1515, and at Scherwiller in 1525, where he achieved glory.
2 CONT He settled in Château-Thierry in Champagne in 1534.
